/* ══ LIGHT MODE ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   Everything in this app resolves through the tokens in @theme, so a light
   theme is a token swap rather than a per-component rewrite. `data-theme` is
   set on <html> by components/nx/ThemeToggle.tsx and pre-applied by an inline
   script in app/layout.tsx so the first paint is already correct.

   THE SLATE RAMP IS INVERTED, and that is the load-bearing part. The dark
   theme remaps --color-slate-* so the app's ~4,700 existing `text-slate-*`
   usages resolve to Nexion's blue-tinted ramp, with 50 lightest and 950
   darkest. Body text is `text-slate-300`. Leaving that direction alone in
   light mode would paint pale text on a white page. So in light mode the ramp
   runs the other way: 50 is the darkest ink and 950 the lightest surface,
   which makes `text-slate-300` a readable dark grey and `bg-slate-900` a
   near-white panel, with no call site touched.

   The ground stays DARKER than the cards here too — the same rule the dark
   theme states — so a white card still reads as lifted off the page. */

/* `:root.nx-portal[data-theme="light"]`, not bare
   `html[data-theme="light"]`: this block re-inverts the SAME tokens
   (--color-slate-*, --color-navy-*, --color-brand-*, --color-white) the
   dark-mode portal block above (`:root.nx-portal { ... }`,
   specificity 0-2-0) already sets — and a bare `html[data-theme="light"]`
   is only 0-1-1, so the dark values silently won this fight REGARDLESS of
   theme, the whole time, for every plain Tailwind utility built on these
   tokens (`text-slate-100`, `text-white`, `bg-navy-900`, …) that never got
   its own component-level override. Confirmed live via getComputedStyle by
   two independent audits, hitting a WizardStickyCart price, a
   WizardReassuranceCard heading, the CookieConsent "Opt out" button, and
   the Build-with-AI hero — all rendering the DARK-mode ink/paper values
   while `data-theme="light"` was active and visibly not helping. The fix
   is the same shape as the dark block's own scoping, plus the attribute
   check, which raises this to 0-3-0 — enough to actually win. */
:root.nx-portal[data-theme="light"] {
  color-scheme: light;

  --color-void: #dde5f2;
  --color-bg: #e9eff8;
  --color-surface: #ffffff;

